\"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"169921f7e19c77ff02b39d96f67d08252548dbf523953515f627434c781d6446","event_uuid":"8a858ed4-95ee-4fab-b65c-37f94ae4a619","position":{"commit_sha":"dfbaeb7d7968c170c5bde7d107d5578504ffb810","position":"1785777718517148001-8a858ed4-95ee-4fab-b65c-37f94ae4a619"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"dc35369a-6e34-424d-af99-7efeb92004fa","comments":[],"created_at":1785776845702404001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[],"description":"## Problem\n\nGitHub code scanning reports TWO OPEN high-severity alerts — the only open alerts on the repository:\n\n    81  py/incomplete-url-substring-sanitization  tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py:249  high\n    82  py/incomplete-url-substring-sanitization  tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py:250  high\n\nBoth are this pattern in `test_a_fallback_entry_endpoint_is_built_against_that_endpoint`:\n\n    assert str(model.models[1].base_url).startswith(\"https://fallback.test\")\n    assert not str(model.models[0].base_url).startswith(\"https://fallback.test\")\n\n`startswith` on a URL is not a host check. `https://fallback.test.evil.example/` satisfies it, because\nthe attacker-controlled part sits AFTER the prefix the assertion pins. The rule is right about the\npattern.\n\n## Honest severity assessment\n\nCodeQL rates these high because the rule cannot distinguish test code from production code. In context\nthe exploitability is nil: the string is a hard-coded constant in a unit test, no untrusted input reaches\nit, and nothing branches on the result except the assertion itself. So the real defect is not a\nvulnerability — it is a WEAK ASSERTION. The test means \"this model was built against that endpoint\" but\nchecks \"the base_url starts with these bytes\", which would also pass for a different host sharing the\nprefix. Fixing it makes the test say what it means AND clears the alert, so the two goals coincide and\nthere is no reason to dismiss instead.\n\nDo NOT resolve this by dismissing the alerts, and do NOT add a suppression comment: the assertion\ngenuinely is weaker than intended.\n\n## Approach\n\nCompare the URL ORIGIN exactly rather than by prefix. Parse both sides with `urllib.parse.urlsplit` and\ncompare `(scheme, netloc)` as a tuple — exact equality has no substring semantics for CodeQL to flag and\nno prefix ambiguity for a reader. `startswith` was presumably chosen because the client normalises the\nconfigured endpoint (e.g. appends a trailing slash), which whole-string equality would break; comparing\nthe parsed origin keeps that tolerance without keeping the weakness.\n\nSingle-source the endpoint constant so the configured value and the asserted value cannot drift.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Both assertions compare the parsed URL ORIGIN (scheme + host) by exact equality, and no\n      `startswith`/`in` substring check against a URL remains anywhere in the file.\n- [ ] The test still FAILS if the fallback entry is built against the provider default instead of the\n      configured endpoint — the property the test protects is preserved, verified by running it.\n- [ ] A host that merely shares the configured endpoint as a prefix\n      (e.g. `https://fallback.test.evil.example`) does NOT satisfy the assertion, pinned by a test or by\n      the construction of the comparison itself.\n- [ ] After the fix lands and CodeQL re-runs, `gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/code-scanning/alerts` reports\n      ZERO open `py/incomplete-url-substring-sanitization` alerts.\n- [ ] No alert is dismissed and no suppression comment is added — the code is changed.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass by exit code; the default selection is green.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"82c9f4cd-f1d7-463b-b35f-a521386c85f9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1086-ca69-007b-4732","ticket_type":"bug","title":"CodeQL high: incomplete URL substring sanitization in the fallback-endpoint test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e0478643-1008-4bfa-9345-50c114587449","b871618c-47cb-4434-9475-e280393f2461","cb2a6e9a-a0be-4654-9d86-ff3a1c4c2a36","6f10a21f-a301-4853-808a-44c7600881ea","82c9f4cd-f1d7-463b-b35f-a521386c85f9","8a858ed4-95ee-4fab-b65c-37f94ae4a619"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785777718517148002,"uuid":"a01e5a4e-27af-4401-8a83-767a646e9875"}